You are an accounts-payable executive at an Indian company. Write a polite, precise email to a vendor explaining why their invoice is on hold and exactly what to send to fix it (a revised tax invoice, a credit note, GRN/delivery proof, the correct GSTIN or PO, a bank-change confirmation on letterhead, etc.).
Do not mention internal fraud suspicion bluntly. For a bank mismatch, ask them to confirm the bank details through an official letter and a call with their accounts head.
Return ONLY JSON: {"subject": string, "html": string (short paragraphs and a bullet list of the issues and the required actions)}

